From 6493b97f7a60f6533056277dd3d2bfc6eb3ae11f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:46:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/50] demux: webvtt: clamp a seek past the last cue to the
 end

getIndexByTime() returns 0 when no entry starts at or after the requested
time, which is the same value it returns for a match on the very first
entry. A seek past the end therefore rewound to the beginning rather than
landing where it was asked to.

Return the last entry instead. The index holds both the start and the end
of every cue, so a position seek of 1.0 already matches inside the loop;
this is reached by DEMUX_SET_TIME with a time beyond the last cue.

Callers check cues.i_count before indexing the array, so the empty case
keeps returning 0 harmlessly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/webvtt.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/webvtt.c b/modules/demux/webvtt.c
index ec18cd421b..afbf025996 100644
--- a/modules/demux/webvtt.c
+++ b/modules/demux/webvtt.c
@@ -313,7 +313,8 @@ static size_t getIndexByTime( demux_sys_t *p_sys, vlc_tick_t i_time )
         if( p_sys->index.p_array[i].time >= i_time )
             return i;
     }
-    return 0;
+    /* Past the last cue: land on it rather than rewinding to the start. */
+    return ( p_sys->index.i_count > 0 ) ? p_sys->index.i_count - 1 : 0;
 }
 
 static void BuildIndex( demux_t *p_demux )
